<%- include('../partials/head', { pageTitle: pageTitle }) %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>

<main class="fb-container fb-main">
  <div class="fb-content">
    <h1 class="fb-title fb-title--small">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="fb-notice">
      <p><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong></p>
      <p>This describes what FieldBrik collects and why, in the terms the site is actually built to. It is not yet a final policy and will be reviewed before the site takes real registrations. Last edited 2 November 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fb-prose">
      <h2>What is collected</h2>
      <ul class="fb-list">
        <li><strong>At registration:</strong> a username, an email address and a password. The password is stored only as a one-way hash and is never readable by staff.</li>
        <li><strong>When you use the site:</strong> the places you build, the items you own, the messages you send, your friends, and the colours you choose for your avatar.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in records:</strong> the time of a sign-in and the browser and network address it came from, kept so a session can be ended and misuse investigated.</li>
        <li><strong>Moderation records:</strong> warnings and restrictions, with the reason and the staff member who issued them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is not collected</h2>
      <p>No payment details are stored on this site. No advertising or tracking networks are embedded. No location, contact list or device data is read.</p>

      <h2>Why it is collected</h2>
      <p>To run your account, show your profile, deliver messages, keep the economy honest, and enforce the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Moderation records exist so that a restriction cannot be evaded by creating a new account.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>One cookie, and only one: the session cookie that keeps you signed in. It is marked HttpOnly so scripts on the page cannot read it, and it is invalidated when you sign out or when the session ends.</p>

      <h2>Who can see what</h2>
      <p>Your username, avatar, description, badges and public creations are visible to anyone. Your email address is never shown to other members. Private messages are readable by you and the recipient, and by staff only when a message is reported or a safety investigation requires it.</p>

      <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>Account data is kept while the account exists. When an account is deleted, profile content is removed and identifying fields are cleared; moderation and transaction records are retained in a form that no longer identifies you, because deleting them would let restrictions and currency records be erased on request.</p>

      <h2>Parents</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/parents">Parents</a> section explains what an account involves, what is asked for at sign-up, and how to ask for an account to be closed.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Privacy requests go through the <a href="/support">support page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
